# Freyalise's Winds replaces only an untap that would happen in the permanent's controller's own untap step (CR 502.3,
# 614.1a; the 2009-10-01 ruling: "first you determine which of your permanents will untap, then you untap them"). Bot1's
# Mana Vault "doesn't untap during your untap step": tapped for mana with Winds out, it gets a wind counter and keeps it
# through Bot1's untap step on turn three. Bot2's Bender's Waterskin, tapped on turn two, untaps "during each other
# player's untap step" - Bot1's, not its controller's - so it untaps on turn three and keeps its wind counter too.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Black Lotus
Mox Emerald
Freyalise's Winds
Mana Vault
Island
Island
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Black Lotus
Bender's Waterskin
Island x25

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Freyalise's Winds.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Mana Vault.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mana Vault.Activate
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Mana Vault.Counters.Wind = 1
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot2.Hand.Bender's Waterskin.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Bender's Waterskin.Activate(Color: Blue)
[T2 Bot2.End]
? Bot2.Battlefield.Bender's Waterskin.Tapped = true
? Bot2.Battlefield.Bender's Waterskin.Counters.Wind = 1
[T3 Bot1.Upkeep]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mana Vault.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Mana Vault.Counters.Wind = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Counters.Wind = (absent)
Bot2.Battlefield.Bender's Waterskin.Tapped = false
Bot2.Battlefield.Bender's Waterskin.Counters.Wind = 1
